.TH PLEB-PLANT-GROWER 6 "2026-08-10" "0.1.0" "Games"
.SH NAME
pleb-plant-grower \- a realtime houseplant you actually have to look after
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pleb-plant-grower
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Plants grow on the wall clock rather than a turn counter. Close the game for a
week and a week of care, or neglect, has happened when you return.
.PP
Runs standalone in a terminal, or embedded in kilix-land. In standalone the
backdrop scene may be swapped or disabled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.PP
The remaining options are headless diagnostics. Each prints a deterministic
report and exits non-zero on the first failed assertion, so all of them are
usable as gates.
.TP
.B \-\-calendar\-test
Date arithmetic, the season window and the local-hour rules. The output is
independent of the host time zone; two runs under different
.B TZ
values compare byte-identical.
.TP
.B \-\-time\-test
The gap matrix: every clock the reconciliation policy survives, including a
backwards wall clock, a reboot, a forged boot id and an
.BR INT64_MIN \-> INT64_MAX
transition.
.TP
.B \-\-care\-test
The care model: derived watering intervals, the symptom ladders and the
cachepot's soggy ticks.
.TP
.B \-\-rules\-test
Verb legality, the four hard refusals and the myth blocklist.
.TP
.BI \-\-selftest " [seed [sim-days]]"
The catch-up engine: the same gap simulated in 15-minute ticks, in one step and
in ragged chunks must agree, and no gap may cost more than 30 days of work.
The output is a pure function of the two arguments, so two runs compare equal.
Defaults to seed 1337 and 400 days. A non-numeric argument is an error.
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-test " dir"
Persistence: the record round trips, then every single-bit flip, truncation and
semantic case is either refused or decodes to a record that re-encodes to
itself \(em and neither outcome ever changes the plant it was handed.
.I dir
must be an absolute path; it is written into and then emptied.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or every assertion in a diagnostic held.
.TP
.B 1
A diagnostic reported a failed assertion.
.TP
.B 2
Unrecognised option, wrong number of arguments, or an unparsable numeric
argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kilix-land (6)
